# round 83 (w102): the single-experiment ablation. The four FBA growth ratios are four DIFFERENT media, so a cell carrying all four reads four experiments at once, which a genotype-by-environment record cannot. The solved flux vector is YPD only (the store provenance says medium YPD), and the gene-rule counts carry no environment at all. These arms drop every column that is not defined within ONE experiment, keeping the YPD ratio: ypdgpr = YPD ratio + YPD vector + counts (against the four-media 0.918); ypdvec = YPD ratio + YPD vector (against 0.908); ypdonly = YPD ratio alone (against the four-media 0.890). Six seeds each, released split.
ESS_SOLVE_TABLE=/scratch/projects/torchcell-scratch/data/torchcell/reference_flux/ess_solve_encodings_YPD_pfbagpr.npz ESS_ARM=pooled ESS_HIDDEN=12 ESS_HEADS=4 ESS_LAYERS=1 ESS_PREPROC=1 ESS_EPOCHS=200 ESS_BATCH=32 ESS_POSW=1 ESS_SPLIT=ess_fcl_val0.2_s0.json.gz ESS_SEED=2700 ESS_TAG=_w102ypdgpr ESS_OUT=w102_ypdgpr_h12l1p1_e200_s2700 ESS_EXTRA='--node-embeddings pathways prot_T5_all --ess-readout fba --ess-fba-media YPD --ess-solve-features pfba --ess-solve-encoding log1p'
